            &title_contents_beg, &title_contents_end)
    &&  off >= lines[line_index + tmp_line_index].end)
```

Here, `lines[line_index + tmp_line_index]` - if `tmp_line_index` is large, `line_index + tmp_line_index` could be out of bounds of the `lines` array. But `tmp_line_index` is bounded by `n_lines - line_index` (since `md_is_link_title` is called with `n_lines - line_index` lines). So `line_index + tmp_line_index <= n_lines - 1`, which is in bounds.

Wait, but `md_is_link_title` returns TRUE with `*p_end_line_index = line_index` where `line_index` is the index within the passed `lines` array. So `tmp_line_index` is at most `n_lines - line_index - 1`. Then `line_index + tmp_line_index <= n_lines - 1`. OK.

